  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures are expected\nthrough early next week.\n\nSurface high pressure continues to build north of the forecast \narea through the end of the week, yielding dry conditions, \nseasonal temperatures, and limited cloud cover. High \ntemperatures will be in the 60s to near 70s each day with \novernight lows in the 30s to mid 40s. \n\nHigh pressure will build southward out of southeastern Canada and \neastern Great Lakes region Saturday through Tuesday. Dry conditions \nare expected each day. There could be some areas of frost Saturday \nmorning. Temperatures will start out chilly Saturday with highs 5 to \n7 degrees below average and highs generally in the upper 50s to \nlower 60s. By Sunday, temperatures will be more seasonable. Monday \nwill encounter highs approaching or reaching the 70 degree mark. By \nTuesday, temperatures may be knocked down to seasonable once again. \nHighs in the middle 60s.",
